<%# Create, on the shared record-page shell - `admin/shared/_record_page`, the same partial the record page
    uses, so a create page is that page with no lifecycle actions and one section. It hand-rolled the same
    column, breadcrumbs and header, which is how six other create pages came to be four different widths.

    **The description says the two things that are not on the page.** It read "You can add money and see
    attendance once the account exists", which was reported as not well written and was worse than that: it
    described *other pages*, in the passive, for a reader who is filling in this one. What they cannot see
    here is what happens on submit - the account is active immediately, and if the password field is left
    blank `MemorablePasswordGenerator` makes one that appears in the flash on the next screen **and nowhere
    else**. That last word is why the notice no longer auto-dismisses; see layouts/_flash.

    The section heading below is `sr_only`. "Details" under "New student" named nothing a reader could not
    already see, and its hint - "Saved when you press Create student" - repeated the button. %>
<%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_page",
           locals: { title: "New student", breadcrumbs: @breadcrumbs,
                     description: "They can sign in straight away. Leave the password blank and one is " \
                                  "generated - the next screen shows it once." } do %>
  <%= render layout: "admin/shared/record_section",
             locals: { title: "Details", sr_only: true } do %>
    <%= render "form" %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
